Treat this project as production level project, So all code sould be in proper structure and optimized

# Project rules
- Follow the existing feature-based structure in `src/`:
  - `components/` for UI components grouped by feature (e.g. `Sidebar`, `EditorArea`, `Header`, `Workbench`).
  - `hooks/` for reusable React hooks.
  - `store/` for global state and Redux slices.
  - `context/` for React context + reducers.
  - `types/` for shared TypeScript types/interfaces.
  - `utils/` for pure utility/helper functions.
  - `data/` for static mock or seed data only.
- Prefer functional React components with hooks; avoid class components.
- Use TypeScript strictly: explicit types for public APIs, avoid `any` unless truly necessary.
- Keep components small and reusable; move shared logic into hooks or utils.
- Do not write inline style; use CSS/Tailwind utility classes and shared style files.
- Preserve existing UI stack conventions (Tailwind + shadcn-style components in `src/components/ui`).
- Use `yarn` for package management and scripts (never use npm).
- Add brief comments only for non-obvious logic; avoid redundant comments.
- Keep imports organized: external libs first, then absolute/internal modules, then relative imports.
- When adding new files, keep naming consistent with current conventions:
  - Components: PascalCase file names (e.g. `StatusBar.tsx`)
  - Hooks: `useXxx.ts`
  - Utils/data: camelCase file names
